        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TakeWalker\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/48/5677_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TakeWalker:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>All right, time to be disappointed and/or confused! :B</p>\n<div>Quote:<br>\n<blockquote>If Blade Battalion Commander is in play, and Battalion Command Center reveals a non-Minion target with 5 or less max HP, it is put into play. It has the Minion keyword because of the Commander.\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n<p>So revealed cards are considered in play? That’s a new one. Can’t think of too many spots where this interaction would happen otherwise, though, so maybe it’s fine as-is.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This has some precedence.  Caspit’s Playground gives keywords to Ongoing cards not in play.  Basically if you meet the criteria to add the keyword it applies whether it’s in play currently, in the deck, or in the trash.</p>",
